sequenceDiagram
    participant R1 as Request 1
    participant R2 as Request 2
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    R1->>DB: SELECT available_seats (= 1)
    R2->>DB: SELECT available_seats (= 1)
    Note over R1,R2: Both read 1 — both pass<br/>the application-level check

    R1->>DB: UPDATE available_seats = 0
    R1->>DB: INSERT INTO bookings
    R2->>DB: UPDATE available_seats = -1
    DB-->>R2: ERROR: violates check constraint
    Note over DB: CHECK (available_seats >= 0)<br/>rejects the second write — INSERT never runs
